  "question": {
    "text": "A convex lens of focal length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> produces images of the same magnification <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>, when an object is kept at two positions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> from the lens. The ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For the given convex lens, focal length, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math></p><p>Magnification of lens in terms of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>When the image is real, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> From Eq. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>75</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Again, when the image is virtual, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;From Eq. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>25</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, the ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>75</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}